sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0243 (swamp role owns serve), ADR 0244 task per fire, Nick 2026-11-02 datastore watch decision. docs/reference/operations.md#swamp-datastore-watch.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: none · swamp-datastore-watch schedule
  %% kind: swamp.datastore_watch
  %% behavior name: swamp-datastore-watch (fixed)
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as Node 209<br/>serve datastore
  Note over SW: Schedule fires<br/>every 15 min · 0 */15 * * * *
  %%> When:
  %%> - every 15 minutes, from the native trigger of `swamp-datastore-watch`, merged on Node 209's serve with the same override that the release Swamp load sets from `swamp/config/swamp-node-schedules.json`
  %%> - serve loads the workflow from the repository with each release, like every workflow
  %%> Not yet:
  %%> - a nested fleet's serve still registers the built-in trigger and the run fails there; a later change removes it, so only the release load sets the schedule
  %%> Not included:
  %%> - no command: no person starts it, and the swamp role installs nothing for it
  %%> - one fire is one task (ADR 0244)
  SW->>N: Measure the datastore<br/>command/shell · measure
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - counts the auto-definitions of each behavior type, the output records, the workflow runs, the data records, the step leases and the grant records in serve's `.swamp`
  %%> - samples serve's CPU over 5 seconds
  %%> Runs as:
  %%> - a swamp worker on Node 209, beside serve; it reads only and changes nothing
  N-->>SW: Counts and CPU<br/>one JSON object
  %%> Returns:
  %%> - `auto_definitions` per type, `outputs`, `workflow_runs`, `data`, `step_leases`, `grants` and `serve_cpu_percent`
  SW-->>GW: Run ended<br/>terminal event · measure
  %%> How the Gateway learns it:
  %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event and reads the step's output; the step never calls the Gateway
  Note over GW: Compare with the bounds<br/>2000 · 50000 · 60000 · 500 · 50%
  %%> Bounds:
  %%> - 2,000 auto-definitions of one type, grant records excepted
  %%> - 50,000 output records
  %%> - 60,000 step leases; bookkeeping keeps them 2 hours, so they level off near 2 hours of dispatches
  %%> - 500 grant records
  %%> - 50% serve CPU
  %%> Why:
  %%> - large auto-definition directories drove serve's CPU past 100% (Lab #4280)
  alt a bound is crossed
    Note over GW: Raise a problem<br/>source swamp · one per bound
    %%> Result:
    %%> - one problem per crossed bound, with the observed value and the bound
    %%> - it becomes ready after a second sighting at least 10 minutes later, like a Doctor finding
  else every value is within bounds
    Note over GW: Resolve open problems<br/>bound_clear
    %%> Result:
    %%> - each open problem whose value is back within its bound is resolved
  else the run failed
    Note over GW: Raise watch failed<br/>watch|failed
    %%> Result:
    %%> - one problem says the datastore is unwatched, with the run id
    %%> - the next fire runs as usual
  end
